dmenu - dynamic menu
====================
dmenu is an efficient dynamic menu for X.


Requirements
------------
In order to build dmenu you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (dmenu is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install dmenu
(if necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running dmenu
-------------
See the man page for details.


Fuzzy matching regression check
-------------------------------
Build and run the headless matching probe with AddressSanitizer and
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer:

    cc -std=c99 -g -O1 -fno-omit-frame-pointer -fsanitize=address,undefined \
        -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE -D_XOPEN_SOURCE=700 -DVERSION='"5.4"' -DXINERAMA \
        -I/usr/include/freetype2 tests/fuzzymatch.c drw.c util.c \
        -lX11 -lXinerama -lfontconfig -lXft -lm -o /tmp/fuzzymatch-check
    ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0 UBSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1 \
        /tmp/fuzzymatch-check a a aab axa

Leak detection is disabled only because initializing linked Fontconfig can
report its known unrelated leak; address and undefined-behavior checks remain
enabled. The probe exercises the real matching implementation without an X
server. Pass `-i`, `-F`, a query, and item labels as arguments to check other
cases.
